        "The alert rule builder places a Metric dropdown, a Condition dropdown, a Threshold text input and an 'Add rule' button on one horizontal row, in that left-to-right order.",
        "The Metric dropdown offers exactly these five options: MRR, Revenue, Churn rate, Conversion rate, Active rate.",
        "The Condition dropdown offers exactly these three options: rises above, falls below, changes by more than.",
        "The 'Add rule' button is disabled while the Threshold input is empty.",
        "The 'Add rule' button is enabled once the Threshold input contains a value.",
        "Clicking 'Add rule' adds exactly one new rule row to the alert rules list.",
        "After a rule is added, the Threshold input is empty.",
        "After a rule is added, the 'Add rule' button is disabled again.",
        "After a rule is added, the Metric and Condition dropdowns still show the values they had when the rule was added.",
        "The alert rules list is seeded with exactly two rules before any user interaction.",
        "The seeded rule 'MRR falls below 60' is in the enabled state.",
        "The seeded rule 'Churn rate rises above 2.5' is in the disabled state.",
        "Each alert rule row displays the rule as a sentence combining its metric, condition and threshold, for example 'MRR falls below 60'.",
        "Each alert rule row contains a switch that changes that rule between enabled and disabled when clicked.",
        "An enabled alert rule's switch uses the app's accent color.",
        "A disabled alert rule's switch is visible and its color differs from an enabled alert rule's switch.",
        "An alert rule row shows no options control until that row is hovered or focused.",
        "Hovering an alert rule row reveals its options control at the right-hand end of the row.",
        "Giving an alert rule row's options control keyboard focus reveals it, just as hovering the row does.",
        "Clicking an alert rule row's options control opens a menu containing an Edit option and a Delete option.",
